From: Stealth Build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 02/05] Rename ChromeDriver $cdc_ marker to a benign prefix

FIX vs. source doc: the doc's diff ADDED a second definition of
kCustomObjectPrefix, which is a C++ redefinition error (two
`const char kCustomObjectPrefix[]` in the same translation unit will
not compile). The correct change REPLACES the value on the existing
line. See QA_REPORT.md #02.

NOTE (scope): this file lives in chrome/test/chromedriver/, i.e. the
ChromeDriver binary, NOT chrome.exe. It only matters for Selenium /
ChromeDriver automation (the `$cdc_...` / `cdc_` document properties
sites probe for). A Playwright/CDP driver does not inject $cdc_ at all,
so this patch is a no-op for the CyberPunch use case. Kept for
completeness; safe to drop if you never drive via chromedriver.

--- a/chrome/test/chromedriver/chrome/custom_v8_functions.cc
+++ b/chrome/test/chromedriver/chrome/custom_v8_functions.cc
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ namespace {

 // Prefix for objects ChromeDriver injects into the page's JS context.
-const char kCustomObjectPrefix[] = "$cdc_";
+const char kCustomObjectPrefix[] = "$_lib_";

 const char kCallFunctionScript[] =
     "(function() {"
